{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/7840-academic-support-advisor-for-student-excellence": {
      "title": "Academic Support Advisor for Student Excellence and Leadership • Human Resources • Beloit College",
      "description": "Academic Support Advisor for Student Excellence and Leadership  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Skip to main content Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. main content Open Side Nav Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Academic Support Advisor for Student Excellence and Leadership Job Posting: Academic Support Advisor for Student Excellence and Leadership Details Item Value Posting Date 10/08/2026 Closing Date Until Filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $20.00-21.00 per Hour Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Occupational Summary: The Student Excellence and Leadership (SEL) Program is a U.S. Department of Education Student Support Services (SSS) TRIO-funded program. Our program is one that believes in focusing on students’ assets and helping them understand how to use those assets to navigate college. The purpose of SEL is to provide academic, personal, career and financial preparation and services to students who are low-income, first-generation college, and/or have a documented disability. The Academic Support Advisor’s (ASA) time will be 100% with SEL. The ASA is responsible for providing functions of financial administration and reporting, to include preparation, tracking, and adjustment of program budgets. Much of the ASA’s time will be devoted to advising and supporting a caseload of approximately 40-50 students, support includes but is not limited to programming, advising, course selection, one-on-one meetings, and career counseling. The ASA will also provide assistance in the management of student enrollment and records, student assessment initiatives, and provides assistance for the program’s Annual Performance Report. This position also provides direct support services to student participants by developing and facilitating participant meetings and events, including the annual Summer Institute and SEL Peer Mentor program. This position is grant-funded, and continuation of the position is dependent upon grant renewal. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Assure that potential students, active participants, and the campus community are fully informed regarding the objectives, opportunities, and responsibilities related to the SSS/SEL program with the development and distribution of promotional materials. Aid in the development and management of the annual Summer Institute program and all other academic programming components to assist students with completing their post-secondary education in compliance with the Department of Education guidelines and the specific programming outlined in the Beloit College SSS grant proposal. Develop and manage the annual Sophomore Impact Institute and/or Professional, Academic & Career (PAC) Institute. Manage the Student Office Assistant Team, including recruiting, selecting, training, supervising, and evaluating assistants in compliance with established college and federal policies and procedures (10-15 students). Interface with college faculty and other student service providers across campus to promote the SEL program, advocate for program participants and collaborate on the development and execution of program and campus services. Synthesize and analyze quantitative and qualitative data and prepare related reports and presentations in a variety of formats. Coordinate and execute programming, including all on- and off-campus events. Develop and facilitate events and programming designed to encourage participant personal and academic success (i.e., Financial Literacy Workshops). Provide direct academic, personal, and financial literacy support services to assigned caseload (35-45 students). Manage the SEL Student Office Assistants team including recruiting, selecting, training, supervising, and evaluating assistants in compliance with established college and federal policies and procedures (10-15 students). Provide feedback for grant-funded proposals and monitor outcomes for grant awards. Represent the SEL program by attending appropriate meetings on and off campus. Remain competent and current through self-directed professional readings, course enrollment, and professional training. Ensure the success of the SEL Program by performing all other duties as assigned. Credentials and Experience: Bachelor’s degree required or an Associate’s degree and 3-5 years of relevant work experience At least 2 years’ experience working with SSS or projects targeted toward low-income, first-generation, and/or disadvantaged students Possess financial administration and budgeting skills Experience analyzing and developing qualitative and quantitative data reports Familiarity with grant-funded programs Experience in student retention programming Experience in academic advising or counseling Relevant life experiences Understanding of issues related to campus climate for populations traditionally underserved by residential liberal arts colleges Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to understand and appreciate the mission of a residential liberal arts college and to work well, in a fast-paced office, with a diverse population of students and their families in a variety of situations. Ability to develop and to contribute to learning and work environments welcoming to people from a diverse variety of backgrounds and experiences. Knowledge of the needs of first generation, low-income, disabled and historically underrepresented students. Knowledge of federal grants, laws, and regulations. Excellent oral and written communication skills, including good command of grammar, punctuation, and spelling. Flexibility and willingness to adapt to changing activities, expectations, and responsibilities. Ability to supervise staff and student employees as well as establish and maintain positive working relationships with all internal and external points of contact. Knowledge of accounting, budgets, and financial aid. Knowledge of customer service standards and the ability to communicate effectively with faculty, administrators, families of students, students, staff, and the general public, including high school personnel. Ability to handle a variety of tasks under pressure. Ability to maintain confidentiality of department records Willingness to look for improvements in personal and office performance and initiate proposals which enhance the work of the office. This job description intends to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please submit your cover letter and resume to the link below. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page Skip to main content This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! × May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11209-assistant-director-of-prospect-management": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Prospect Management",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Prospect Management  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Assistant Director of Prospect Management Job Posting: Assistant Director of Prospect Management Details Item Value Posting Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $45,000-50,000 per Year Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Occupational Summary: The Office of Advancement & Alumni Engagement’s mission is to inform external constituents of the College’s mission and goals; to involve them as volunteers in fulfilling its mission; and to inspire them to invest their resources in support of current objectives and future dreams. The Assistant Director of Prospect Management will support our fundraising efforts through prospect research, data analysis, and assisting with portfolio management. The Assistant Director will collaborate closely with the Senior Director of Advancement & Campaign Manager and the Advancement Operations team. By providing insights and research, the Assistant Director will directly support our fundraising goals, initiatives, the campaign, and the mission of Beloit College ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 1. Must successfully manage multiple projects with competing and/or shifting priorities while maintaining a high degree of professionalism and confidentiality. 2. Use various software tools to analyze data, synthesize its findings, and share results in clear and compelling presentations. 3. Analyze prospect pools and ensure prospects are assigned in accordance with department guidelines. 4. Document fundraising metrics and other division reporting as identified by the Senior Director. 5. Provide support with the creation of constituent profiles. 6. Monitor constituent alerts on pertinent activity. 7. Investigate fundraising initiatives to determine if a sufficient number of prospects can be identified to meet funding goals, utilize wealth screenings to identify prospects for major gifts, planned gifts, and annual gifts, engage in data mining to identify giving trends, and perform qualitative and quantitative analysis to evaluate each identified prospect’s potential and propensity to financially support the college. 8. Monitor, analyze, and report on progress toward goals. 9. Keep abreast of new products, resources, technologies, and methodologies to enhance work. 10. Collaborate with the Senior Director to develop, document, and maintain policies for Advancement and Alumni Engagement. 11. Safeguard the confidentiality of donor information at all times, exercise discretion, and adhere to the ethical and confidentiality policies and guidelines of the college and the Association of Professional Researchers for Advancement (APRA). 12. Become cross-trained in all areas within the Advancement Operations unit to ensure continuity across business functions. 13. Belief in the mission and strong ethical conduct are essential. Contribute to building a world-class culture of philanthropy by taking responsibility for other special tasks as requested. 15. Perform other duties as assigned. Credentials and Experience: 1. Minimum of two-five years’ experience in prospect management, research, data analysis, or other similar field, preferably in an academic or nonprofit healthcare or related industry setting. 2. Bachelor’s degree preferred. 3. Other transferable skills will be considered. 4. Experience with relational databases and their structure. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Advanced Proficiency in MS Word, Excel, and fundraising software; experience with Blackbaud RE CRM is preferred. 2. Experience with research tools such as iWave, LiveAlumni, and AlumniFinder also beneficial, as well as Power BI to create custom reports and dashboards. 3. Ability to meet deadlines and carry out multiple projects simultaneously. 4. Ability to manage complex processes and procedures with strong attention to detail and accuracy.Experience with data analytics and reporting is strongly preferred. 5. Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. 6. Curiosity and skill in searching and retrieving information from online sources and database products; ability to interpret financial and biographical data from a variety of sources. 7. Ability to exercise judgment and maintain confidentiality on a wide spectrum of topics and issues for which discretion is required. How to Apply Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please submit your cover letter and resume to the link provided below. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11159-director-of-career-works": {
      "title": "Director of Career Works",
      "description": "Director of Career Works  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Director of Career Works Job Posting: Director of Career Works Details Item Value Posting Date 09/02/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $70,000-75,000 per Year Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Occupational Summary: The Director of Career Works implements an entrepreneurial vision to advance career readiness throughout the student experience. This leadership position develops, manages, and assesses an integrated student development operation that delivers innovative, user-friendly programs and support to all students, alumni, employers, faculty, staff, and community partners. The Director of Career Works reports to the Provost & Dean of the College and collaborates with colleagues in Community Connections/Impact Beloit, the Advancement division, faculty, and staff, as well as with external partners, including alumni and employers. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Center Management & Assessment Develops and leads short- and long-range operating plans, including budgets, programs, services, personnel, technology, and space. Recruits, hires, supervises, and supports the ongoing professional development of Career Works professional staff. Directs the collection, analysis, and use of data for center assessment, including student engagement metrics, first destination outcomes, and required institutional and regulatory reporting. Oversees and coordinates across administrative units transportation for student internship placements. Student Advising Provides individualized advising to students on career development, experiential learning, and post-graduate planning. Connects students with alumni mentors and professional networks through collaboration with Advancement, faculty, and employer partners. Maintains current knowledge of career development theory, workforce and community engagement trends, and best practices in alumni and employer relations. Strategic Planning Develops and sustains the mission and vision of a comprehensive career center aligned with the curriculum, workforce trends, and the College’s mission and commitment to supporting student success. Collaborates with faculty and staff in Academic Affairs and Student Life to advance career development and student success initiatives. Partners with Advancement/Alumni Engagement to develop opportunities for alumni involvement in career development programming. Partners with School and Center Directors to improve coordination and efficiency in advising, alumni engagement, and programming. Leads the design, implementation, and transition of pilot programs and courses, transferring ongoing execution to appropriate faculty or staff once initiatives are stabilized. Represents the college as needed at external events and professional associations. Programming Leads the development and management of the annual calendar of career and professional development programming for students. Provides strategic oversight for large-scale career and professional development initiatives, including career fairs, boot camps, retreats, and related events. Instruction May teach for-credit internship and Impact Beloit courses as appropriate to support Career Works programming and student development. Provides leadership and vision for partner development, employer engagement, and student placements within the Concierge Internship Program and similar programs. Credentials and Experience: Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree preferred; plus at least seven years of progressively responsible experience in career development, community engagement, volunteer management, or related field. Experience working with undergraduate students of diverse backgrounds; experience in liberal arts settings preferred. Experience working with graduate students is a plus. Experience developing and implementing career development, community-engagement, or other student development programs. Experience developing programs and services that support students from a variety of backgrounds and experiences. Experience hiring, training, supervising, and evaluating employees. Experience with budget development and management. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Understanding of and commitment to a liberal arts education and the role of experiential education, career development and preparation, and community engagement in the liberal arts environment. Ability to develop and to contribute to learning and work environments welcoming to people from a variety of backgrounds and experiences. Ability to work collaboratively and professionally with multiple individuals, departments across campus, and external stakeholders. Ability to cultivate relationships with potential internship sites, employers, alumni, and community partners. Expertise with and understanding of effective approaches, emerging trends, and innovations to academic, professional, and career development for undergraduate students. Knowledge of federal and state employment laws and regulations, and public sector employment policies and procedures relevant to career development, internships, employment, and experiential learning. Demonstrated ability in the areas of outreach, marketing, and collaboration. Strong written and oral communication, advising, and collaboration skills. Excellent problem-solving and innovation skills. Proficiency with technological tools used in career development. Computer proficiency, including experience with Google Workspace (Gmail, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Meet, Chat), Microsoft Windows environment, Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), computer assisted career guidance/assessment programs, online career information management programs, and online career research methods. Ability to oversee recordkeeping and reporting systems and procedures. Flexibility and willingness to perform other job-related duties and responsibilities as assigned. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please submit your cover letter and resume to the link provided below. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/9209-executive-assistant-to-vp-advancement-and-alumni": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to VP Advancement and Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Executive Assistant to VP Advancement and Alumni Engagement  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Executive Assistant to VP Advancement and Alumni Engagement Job Posting: Executive Assistant to VP Advancement and Alumni Engagement Details Item Value Posting Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date Until Filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $47,000-50,000 per Year Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Occupational Summary: The Executive Assistant provides executive-level support to the Vice President for Advancement and Alumni Engagement. This position performs a broad array of office responsibilities in support of the Vice President and the Division, including managing the office’s budget and workflow, and facilitating and managing communication to and from the Vice President and Division to a variety of constituents, including alumni, trustees, faculty, staff, and students, with integrity, trust, and discretion. The Executive Assistant actively fosters cooperation and communication among individuals and teams within the Division, utilizes sound judgment in setting priorities and making decisions, and manages multiple priorities in a fast-paced office environment. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Maintain the Vice President’s calendar and assist with communications, including opening, routing, and prioritizing incoming mail, email, and other correspondence while exercising discretion in formulating appropriate responses for the Vice President’s review. Ensure a timely flow of information to and from the Vice President. This includes expert prioritization, handling extremely confidential and sensitive information, and maintaining highly professional contact with on- and off-campus constituencies on behalf of the Vice President. Actively foster cooperation and communication between individuals and teams within the Division. Manage the budget for the Division, including monthly budget reconciliation, the Vice President’s travel expenses, credit card statements, and submitting the division’s budget/expense requisitions. Assist with the preparation and facilitation of the Vice President’s meetings with the College President, Senior Staff, Division members, and campus colleagues. Manage Vice President’s domestic and international travel arrangements (scheduling of appointments, hotel/flight/car/train reservations; create itineraries/maps/logistics and meeting resources). Schedule meetings of various sizes and complexities with key volunteers and investors. Prepare and enter the Vice President’s action reports related to engagement and involvement with alumni, friends, and parents of Beloit College. Provide general office support, including ordering supplies, onboarding new colleagues to the Division’s general operating procedures and culture of the team, and providing general oversight of student workers. Prepare and initiate agendas, minutes, reports, and supporting materials for Board of Trustees committees staffed by the Vice President. Contribute to an organization that places a high value on trust and teamwork, emphasizing cooperation and collegiality to foster an exceptionally positive and productive work environment. Maintain the highest standards of fiscal, ethical, and professional conduct. Frequently exercise independent judgment and function with minimum supervision. Contribute to building a culture of philanthropy at Beloit College by taking responsibility for other special tasks as requested. Credentials and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent required. A Bachelor’s degree is desirable. Proven track record of more than five years in a dependable, high-responsibility position. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: The ability to work with diverse groups of people sensitively and professionally. Advanced levels of proficiency in the Microsoft and Google Suite of products required. Capacity to learn database systems required. Excellent oral and written communication skills, including a command of grammar, punctuation, and spelling, and exceptional proofreading ability. Skilled at organizing and prioritizing workload while maintaining flexibility to handle interruptions and shifting demands. Ability to build strong, respectful communication with diverse stakeholders, including Board members, alumni, faculty, staff, students, and community members. Willingness and ability to maintain the confidentiality of all College matters. Demonstrates composure and professionalism in high-pressure environments. Self-motivated and able to work independently with minimal guidance. Familiarity with college or university administration and an understanding of higher education and how it functions is preferred. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be constructed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply To apply send a cover letter, resume, and names and contact information of three professional references. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/8471-housekeeper": {
      "title": "Housekeeper • Human Resources • Beloit College",
      "description": "Housekeeper  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Skip to main content Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. main content Open Side Nav Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Housekeeper Job Posting: Housekeeper Details Item Value Posting Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary $15.03 per Hour Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The Beloit Advantage: Outstanding Benefits Package – Includes health, dental, vision, retirement contributions, and college-paid life insurance. Tuition Remission & Educational Opportunities – Take classes at Beloit College for personal enrichment or toward a degree, with tuition benefits for eligible employees and their dependents. Professional Learning & Development – Access workshops, conferences, and training to support your growth and career advancement. Generous Paid Time Off (PTO) – Includes generous paid time off plus a brief winter break to recharge. Occupational Summary: The Facilities Departments are essential contributors to the residential teaching and learning experience at Beloit College. The operation, quality, cleanliness, and appearance of the residential, academic, and administrative spaces on campus help to create a healthy and pleasant living, learning, and working environment. The housekeeper position requires the ability to effectively interact with diverse faculty, staff, and students while conducting a variety of duties relating to the upkeep of over 80 campus buildings as directed by a supervisor. The ability to learn and understand how the housekeeping department contributes to residential living as part of the liberal arts experience is an important aspect for success in this position. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Performs cleaning tasks in assigned areas in accordance with established procedures and safety rules. Routine cleaning tasks will include: Collects and removes trash and cleanup litter (inside and outside). Cleans/washes/disinfects restrooms and shower rooms, elevator interiors, individual room phones, room trash baskets and trash collection container. Dusting/cleaning walls, doors, furniture, drapes and windows inside and out. Sweeping, vacuuming, mopping, scrubbing, and carpet cleaning where needed. Replaces burned out light bulbs and clean the light fixtures. Other duties include: Care of hard surfaced floors and woodwork including stripping and refinishing where and when needed. Assists with snow removal as directed by supervisor. Assists with moving and setting up furnishings and equipment as assigned (this includes college event set-ups). Frequently exercise judgment with regard to appropriate chemical supplies and equipment used daily. Keeps equipment clean and operating properly and report malfunctioning equipment to supervisor by phone, in person or on a work order. Immediately reports any unsafe or unusual conditions and any evidence of damage or need of repair to supervisor and on a work order. Completes work orders and project requests as assigned by supervisor. Completes and maintain supply order requests and insure an adequate supply of stock is maintained in the building. Works as part of a team as assigned by supervisor. Assists or work with other facilities personnel when directed by supervisor. Trains, works with, and/or coordinates the responsibilities of facilities student employees. Maintains security of keys and lock and unlock areas as required. Accomplishes assigned custodial tasks while working within the framework of OSHA safety regulations that govern procedures of personal safety, chemical, and equipment usage. Credentials and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent. Previous housekeeping operation background/experience preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of housekeeping operations. Knowledge of customer service standards and procedures in housekeeping operations including organizing and prioritizing work assignments. Ability to develop and foster a cooperative work environment. Flexibility in all phases of tasks with the ability to accept, manage and incorporate change. Ability to develop, and to contribute to, learning and work environments welcoming to people from a diverse variety of backgrounds and experiences. Outstanding interpersonal and community relations skills and the ability to listen, communicate and work effectively within a diverse community . Ability to understand and appreciate the mission of a residential liberal arts college. Knowledge and understanding of OSHA, fire and life safety standards and rules, regulations and procedures for handling hazardous materials. Ability to use hand and power tools applicable to housekeeping operations. Ability to read and write and to follow both oral and written instructions. Special Requirements: Must possess a valid driver’s license and be reachable for on-call for emergencies. Shares on-call responsibilities. Physical Requirements: Requires full range of body motion including: Ability to lift 40 pounds, 30 pounds frequently and independently. Ability to perform bending squatting, twisting, crawling, and climbing. Ability to stand or walk for long periods of time and freely traverse campus. Ability to climb stairs and ladders up to 10 feet. Visual ability to safely and effectively operate equipment. Hearing and speaking abilities to effectively communicate through earpiece and in person. Ability to work outside in all weather conditions. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be constructed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Application review will begin immediately and continue until positions are filled. Begin Your Application: Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page Skip to main content This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! × May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11197-instruction-and-student-engagement-librarian": {
      "title": "Instruction and Student Engagement Librarian • Human Resources • Beloit College",
      "description": "Instruction and Student Engagement Librarian  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Skip to main content Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. main content Open Side Nav Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Instruction and Student Engagement Librarian Job Posting: Instruction and Student Engagement Librarian Details Item Value Posting Date 10/08/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $54,000-56,000 per Year Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Occupational Summary: This role is responsible for supporting the teaching, learning, and research of Beloit College students, faculty, and staff, with particular focus on collaborating with academic and student service departments. This role engages in the design, delivery, and assessment of programming, resources, and instruction to support curricular and co-curricular students needs. The Instruction and Student Engagement Librarian provides specialized research support, instruction, outreach, and collection development for a number of departments and schools. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Research and Instruction Design, develop, facilitate, and assess innovative information and digital literacy outreach programs and associated learning activities aligned with curricular and co-curricular programs. Cultivate and maintain relationships with academic and student service departments to encourage collaboration in research and instruction. Identify, implement and promote student success through information literacy, digital literacy, and academic skill initiatives. Participate in an ongoing, innovative program of academic and research support for students in collaboration with LITS staff. Provide reference and research support in a variety of modalities for students, faculty, and staff. Engage in collection development in collaboration with faculty, students, and staff. Maintains and updates research guides. Government Documents Serves as Federal Depository Coordinator, ensuring compliance with legal requirements and providing relevant reference and instruction services. Maintains the federal and state government documents collection; prepares reports required by the Federal Depository Library Program; assesses holdings, print retention, and online access to materials. Develops and implements an outreach program to promote awareness of government resources to the campus and local community. Collaborates with department and college stakeholders to educate about government documents. Outreach and Engagement Creates informative and engaging displays on a diverse range of topics relevant to the community. Creates and coordinates outreach and programming opportunities, collaborates with campus stakeholders, and participates in campus events. Facilitates assessment initiatives to inform decision-making around programming, outreach, and library services. Collaborates with student service departments and student life units Fosters user focused collaboration, diversity, equity, and inclusiveness. Professional Service and Engagement Serves on library and campus community meetings, teams, or committees. Engages in local, regional, national, and/or international professional societies. Contributes to the profession through organizational work, presentations, and/or publishing. Credentials and Experience: ALA-Accredited Master’s Degree in Library Science or international equivalent Applicants nearing completion of the MLS degree may be considered; however, degree must be completed prior to the anticipated start date in January 2027. Coursework or experience in instruction, reference, and outreach. Knowledge of current pedagogy trends, instructional and research methods, assessment, outreach, and information and digital literacy principles preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong commitment to engaging users and providing excellent service. Demonstrated ability to work in a rapidly-changing environment. Ability to develop and maintain excellent, collaborative working relationships with faculty and staff. Commitment to fostering an equitable and inclusive workplace, and ability to work effectively in a diverse academic setting. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities. The physical demands of this position include: The physical demands of the position include: Visual ability to safely and effectively operate equipment, read computer screens, and printed materials; Hearing and speaking abilities to effectively communicate through the telephone and in person; Ability to lift up to 30 lbs. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please submit your cover letter and resume to the link provided below. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page Skip to main content This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! × May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/1469-security-officer": {
      "title": "Security Officer • Human Resources • Beloit College",
      "description": "Security Officer  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Skip to main content Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. main content Open Side Nav Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Security Officer Job Posting: Security Officer Details Item Value Posting Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary $17.00 per Hour Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Help Create a Safe and Welcoming Community Beloit College is seeking an unarmed Security Officer to help provide a safe, inclusive, and supportive environment where students, faculty, staff, and visitors can thrive. This position combines campus safety responsibilities with customer service, emergency response, problem-solving, and community engagement. Officers serve as trusted resources who respond to emergencies, assist community members, and help ensure the campus remains safe and welcoming. We welcome applicants with a variety of backgrounds and experiences. Experience in security, customer service, hospitality, military service, emergency response, facilities, or higher education is beneficial but not required. Training will be provided; however, the position requires the ability to exercise independent judgment, make timely decisions, and follow College policies and Standard Operating Procedures. The Security Officer reports to the Director of Security. This is a full-time position consisting of four 10-hour shifts per week (40 hours), typically from 6:00 p.m. to 4:00 a.m. Employees can generally expect a consistent schedule. Overtime is uncommon but may occasionally be required to meet operational needs or respond to emergencies. The Beloit Advantage Outstanding Benefits Package – Includes optional health, dental, vision, retirement contributions, and College-paid life insurance. Tuition Remission & Educational Opportunities – Take classes at Beloit College for personal enrichment or toward a degree, with tuition benefits for eligible employees and their dependents. Generous time Off – Includes generous Paid Time Off, Sick Bank Leave, plus a brief winter break to recharge and enjoy the season. Meaningful and varied work – Make a difference supporting students, employees, and visitors in a collaborative campus environment. Paid training and professional development - Includes paid CPR/First Aid/AED certification, and ongoing training. Stable full-time overnight schedule – Occasional OT based on calendar work week, 2.5x regular pay for Holidays Worked. Equipment Provided – Uniforms, radio, and vehicle for off-site patrols. Key Responsibilities Community Safety Patrol campus buildings and grounds while maintaining a visible, welcoming presence. Assist students, employees, and visitors with directions, escorts, lockouts, and other service requests. Secure and unlock buildings and identify safety hazards or maintenance concerns. Emergency Response Respond to medical, behavioral, fire, weather, and other emergencies. Coordinate with campus departments and public safety partners. Activate emergency notifications and assist during critical incidents. Operations & Administration Complete accurate typed reports and preliminary investigations. Conduct monthly safety inspections and equipment checks. Perform dispatcher duties and other related responsibilities as assigned. Who Succeeds in This Role? Enjoys helping others Communicates professionally Remains calm under pressure Works independently and uses sound judgment Is dependable, observant, and detail-oriented Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Valid U.S. driver’s license and insurable under College guidelines. - DUIs, reckless driving, and speeding +15MPH are instant disqualifications. You must have had 2 or fewer moving violations in the past 5 years. Ability to patrol campus on foot, work outdoors in all weather conditions, and perform the physical duties of the position. Ability to obtain CPR/AED and First Aid certification within one year of hire. Successful completion of a background check. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and should not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Application review will begin immediately and continue until positions are filled. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page Skip to main content This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! × May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11184-academic-fieldwork-coordinator-and-faculty-of": {
      "title": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty of Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty of Occupational Therapy  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty of Occupational Therapy Job Posting: Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Faculty of Occupational Therapy Details Item Value Posting Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $85,000-90,000 per Year Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The opportunity Beloit College invites applications for a founding Academic Fieldwork Coordinator (AFWC) and faculty member for its new Master of Science in Occupational Therapy (OT) program. This is an opportunity to design a fieldwork education program from the ground up and to build the clinical partnerships, structures, and culture that will define students’ transition from classroom to practice at a liberal arts institution that genuinely values faculty expertise and intellectual vision. The founding AFWC will have significant latitude to develop a fieldwork program that is both rigorously ACOTE-compliant and distinctively Beloit. We are seeking an occupational therapist who understands that fieldwork is not an add-on to the curriculum; it is where professional identity, clinical reasoning, and community-responsive practice come together. The program’s animating commitments include experiential and community-based learning as core program features rather than afterthoughts; attention to the occupational therapy workforce needs of south-central Wisconsin and the broader region, including Chicago, Milwaukee, and Madison; interprofessional and interdisciplinary education, consistent with Beloit’s institution-wide pedagogical identity; and a commitment to serving underserved communities. About Beloit College Beloit College is a selective liberal arts college in Beloit, Wisconsin. Nationally recognized for intellectual rigor and innovation, Beloit was ranked #18 among the nation’s most innovative schools by U.S. News & World Report in 2026. Its graduates are known for their capacity to think across disciplines, engage with complexity, and connect knowledge to real-world impact. The School of Health Sciences, established in 2023, reflects Beloit’s commitment to preparing health professionals who are not only clinically excellent but broadly educated and community-minded. Interdisciplinary collaboration, experiential learning, and community-based practice are foundational to everything we do. The Master of Science in Occupational Therapy will lead the School’s growing portfolio of graduate programs as it pursues accreditation from the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE). Role and Responsibilities The Academic Fieldwork Coordinator is the full-time faculty member appointed to the occupational therapy program who is responsible for the development, implementation, management, and evaluation of fieldwork education, as required under ACOTE Standards. This is a 12-month faculty position with documented release time sufficient to ensure the needs of the fieldwork program are met, and with teaching responsibilities commensurate with the coordinator’s expertise and program needs. The Academic Fieldwork Coordinator reports to the Program director for the Occupational Therapy Program. Fieldwork Program Development and Management Design, implement, manage, and evaluate the program’s fieldwork education, including Level I and Level II fieldwork experiences Establish, formalize, and sustain fieldwork placement partnerships across the region to ensure sufficient, high-quality sites for all students Develop and maintain fieldwork agreements, memoranda of understanding, and site documentation in coordination with institutional leadership Develop the fieldwork manual and the policies, procedures, and student assessment systems that govern fieldwork Prepare, orient, and support fieldwork educators at clinical sites, including training in the roles and responsibilities of a fieldwork educator ACOTE Compliance Ensure the program’s compliance with the fieldwork requirements of ACOTE Standards. Contribute fieldwork content and documentation to the Candidacy Application, Self-Study, and ongoing accreditation reporting Maintain the data, records, and evaluation systems that demonstrate fieldwork outcomes and continuous improvement Teaching and Faculty Responsibilities Teach occupational therapy courses in areas of professional expertise as needed by the program Advise students and participate in student assessment, retention, and professional-behavior processes Contribute to curriculum development, program evaluation, and faculty governance Community and Institutional Engagement Build and sustain relationships with clinical partners, site supervisors, and community organizations Collaborate with faculty across the School of Health Sciences and the broader College to advance interprofessional and interdisciplinary programming Represent the program in professional occupational therapy organizations and within the institution Required Qualifications Candidates must meet the ACOTE academic fieldwork coordinator requirements for a master’s-degree-level occupational therapy program. Specifically, the successful candidate must: Be an occupational therapist who is licensed or otherwise regulated as an occupational therapist in Wisconsin, or be eligible for Wisconsin licensure Hold a minimum of a master’s degree awarded by an institution accredited by a USDE-recognized institutional accrediting agency Have at least two years of documented experience in the field of occupational therapy, which must include clinical practice experience as an occupational therapist and professional experience as a fieldwork educator, or documented training in the roles and responsibilities of a fieldwork educator Be prepared to take responsibility for the program’s compliance with the fieldwork requirements of ACOTE Standards. Beyond ACOTE requirements, Beloit College requires: An earned doctoral degree (OTD, PhD, EdD, or related), which aligns with ACOTE Standards for full-time occupational therapy faculty who teach OT content Strong organizational and administrative skills, including the ability to manage many clinical relationships and detailed documentation simultaneously Demonstrated ability to build and maintain community and clinical partnerships Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse communities Capacity to function effectively in a startup environment: the program is being built from the ground up, and the coordinator will likewise be building its fieldwork infrastructure from the ground up. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience as an academic fieldwork coordinator or in fieldwork site coordination Experience developing fieldwork or experiential-education programs, including involvement in ACOTE accreditation processes Experience with rural or community-based practice, interprofessional education, or health disparities Experience recruiting, teaching, and mentoring diverse graduate student populations Appointment and Compensation This is a full-time, 12-month faculty position with documented release time for fieldwork coordination. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. The anticipated start date is June 1, 2027, consistent with the program’s accreditation timeline. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials through Beloit College’s online application system: Cover letter addressing qualifications and vision for the fieldwork program Current curriculum vitae, including clinical, teaching, and fieldwork-coordination experience Statement (2–3 pages) describing experience with fieldwork or experiential education, clinical partnership development, and, if applicable, accreditation Teaching philosophy statement Names and contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission) The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Begin Your Application Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11189-assistant-professor-of-economics": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business/Finance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Business/Finance  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Assistant Professor of Business/Finance Job Posting: Assistant Professor of Business/Finance Details Item Value Posting Date 09/28/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Tenure Track Full Time Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The Beloit College Department of Economics and Business invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning fall 2027. Preference is given to candidates who have completed or anticipate completion of a Ph.D. in Business Administration, Finance, or related fields. Teaching responsibilities may include Accounting, Corporate Finance, Investment and Portfolio Management, and Personal Finance (among others). Faculty at Beloit College have multiple opportunities to contribute to all-college programs, including the Advanced Mentoring Program for first-year students, our career-oriented schools, and our global engagement program. Participation in campus governance is an expectation of employment. Opportunities to collaborate with colleagues outside the department and with community partners are plentiful. Located in a diverse community close to Madison, Milwaukee, and Chicago, Beloit attracts students from across the United States and world. The college emphasizes excellence in teaching, advising, learning beyond the traditional classroom, international perspectives, and collaborative research among students and faculty. We are recognized as one of the Colleges That Change Lives. Complete applications include a cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy, a CV, a recent example of research, and 3 letters of recommendation. Teaching evaluations are strongly suggested. The application deadline is November 15th. How to Apply Begin Your Application Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11190-assistantassociate-professor-of-economics": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics Job Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics Details Item Value Posting Date 09/28/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Tenure Track Full Time Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The Beloit College Department of Economics and Business invites applications for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor beginning fall 2027. A strong commitment to excellence in teaching is necessary. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching macroeconomics (principles and intermediate), microeconomics (principles and intermediate), quantitative methods, econometrics, game theory and/or math econ, sports economics, and other electives. Faculty at Beloit College have multiple opportunities to contribute to all-college programs, including the Advanced Mentoring Program for first-year students, our career-oriented schools, and our global engagement program. Participation in campus governance is an expectation of employment. Opportunities to collaborate with colleagues outside the department and with community partners are plentiful. Located in a diverse community close to Madison, Milwaukee, and Chicago, Beloit attracts students from across the United States and world. The college emphasizes excellence in teaching, advising, learning beyond the traditional classroom, international perspectives, and collaborative research among students and faculty. We are recognized as one of the Colleges That Change Lives. Complete applications include a cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy, a CV, a recent example of research, and 3 letters of recommendation. Teaching evaluations are strongly suggested. The application deadline is November 15th. How to Apply Begin Your Application Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11178-director-of-clinical-training-core-faculty-and": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Training, Core Faculty and Clinical Coordinator",
      "description": "Director of Clinical Training, Core Faculty and Clinical Coordinator  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Director of Clinical Training, Core Faculty and Clinical Coordinator Job Posting: Director of Clinical Training, Core Faculty and Clinical Coordinator Details Item Value Posting Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $80,000-84,000 per Year Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The opportunity Beloit College invites applications for a founding core faculty member who will also serve as Clinical Coordinator (Director of Clinical Training) for its new Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program. This is an opportunity to build the program’s clinical training infrastructure from the ground up and to establish the practicum and internship partnerships, structures, and culture that will define students’ transition from classroom to practice at a liberal arts institution that genuinely values faculty expertise and intellectual vision. We are seeking a counselor educator who understands that clinical training is where professional identity, ethical practice, and community-responsive counseling come together. This person will carry the responsibilities of a core faculty member and, in addition, lead the coordination of the program’s practicum and internship experiences. The program’s animating commitments include: social justice as a foundational orientation, embedded throughout the curriculum and clinical training; attention to underserved communities and the mental health workforce needs of south-central Wisconsin and the broader region, including Chicago, Milwaukee, and Madison; interprofessional and interdisciplinary education, consistent with Beloit’s institution-wide pedagogical identity; and community-based, experiential learning as a core program feature. About Beloit College Beloit College is a selective liberal arts college in Beloit, Wisconsin. Nationally recognized for intellectual rigor and innovation, Beloit was ranked #18 among the nation’s most innovative schools by U.S. News & World Report in 2026. Its graduates are known for their capacity to think across disciplines, engage with complexity, and connect knowledge to real-world impact. The School of Health Sciences, established in 2023, reflects Beloit’s commitment to preparing health professionals who are not only clinically excellent but broadly educated and community-minded. Interdisciplinary collaboration, experiential learning, and community-based practice are foundational to everything we do. The MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling is the School’s first graduate-level program, a significant milestone and a serious institutional commitment. Role and Responsibilities This position is a core counselor education faculty member, as defined under the 2024 CACREP Standards, who additionally serves as the program’s practicum and internship coordinator. This is a 12-month faculty position with teaching, advising, scholarship, and service responsibilities, plus dedicated responsibility and support for clinical coordination. The position reports to the CMHC Program Director. Clinical Training Coordination Serve as the program’s practicum and internship coordinator, responsible for the coordination of practicum and internship experiences in the Clinical Mental Health Counseling specialized practice area Establish, formalize, and sustain clinical site partnerships and affiliation agreements across the region to ensure sufficient, high-quality placements for all students Recruit, orient, evaluate, and support site supervisors, including verifying supervisor qualifications and providing supervisor training consistent with CACREP requirements Manage student placement, clinical documentation, liability and site requirements, and respond to inquiries regarding practicum and internship Monitor student progress in field experiences and coordinate clinical gatekeeping with program faculty Teaching and Curriculum Teach across the CMHC curriculum in areas of professional expertise, including clinical and skills coursework Provide clinical instruction and supervision as assigned Contribute to curriculum development, program accreditation, and continuous improvement consistent with the 2024 CACREP Standards Student Development, Scholarship, and Service Advise and mentor students, supporting professional identity development and well-being Maintain sustained professional engagement through scholarship, professional development, service, advocacy, or ongoing counseling practice Contribute to CACREP self-study preparation, program evaluation, and ongoing compliance; represent the program with community partners and professional organizations Required Qualifications Candidates must meet the 2024 CACREP core counselor education faculty requirements. Per those standards, core faculty hold a full-time appointment to the program and must have one of the following: An earned doctoral degree in counselor education, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program; or A related doctoral degree and full-time employment as a faculty member in a counselor education program for a minimum of one full academic year before July 1, 2013; or Full-time doctoral-level faculty employment in a CORE-accredited master’s program prior to July 1, 2017; or Graduation from a rehabilitation counseling doctoral program prior to January 1, 2018 In addition, all candidates must demonstrate the following per 2024 CACREP Standards: Sustained membership in professional counseling organizations Relevant professional counseling credentials (e.g., LPC, LCPC, or equivalent Wisconsin licensure or eligibility for Wisconsin licensure) Evidence of sustained professional engagement through professional development, service and advocacy, ongoing counseling practice, or research and scholarly activity in counseling For the clinical coordination responsibilities, candidates must additionally meet CACREP requirements for practicum and internship coordinators, including a master’s degree in counseling or a related profession (met by the doctoral core-faculty qualification above). Beyond CACREP requirements, Beloit College requires: Clinical practice experience as a counselor and familiarity with clinical supervision Demonstrated ability to build and maintain community and clinical partnerships and to manage detailed placement documentation Demonstrated commitment to social justice, multicultural counseling, and working with marginalized and underserved communities Capacity to function effectively in a startup environment, building clinical training infrastructure from the ground up Preferred Qualifications Identification with a Clinical Mental Health Counseling specialized practice area Prior experience as a clinical coordinator, director of clinical training, or field placement coordinator Approved clinical supervisor credential (e.g., Wisconsin-approved supervisor or ACS) or eligibility Experience with CACREP accreditation processes, rural mental health, or integrated behavioral health Experience recruiting and mentoring diverse graduate student populations Appointment and Compensation This is a full-time, 12-month core counselor education faculty position with documented support and release time for clinical coordination. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials through Beloit College’s online application system: Cover letter addressing qualifications, vision for clinical training, and fit with the program’s mission Current curriculum vitae, including clinical, supervision, teaching, and coordination experience Teaching philosophy statement Statement describing experience with clinical site development, supervision, and work with underserved communities Names and contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission) Review of applications will begin in October, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Beloit College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to building a diverse and inclusive faculty. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. How to Apply Begin Your Application Review of applications will begin in October, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11183-faculty-clinical-mental-health-counseling": {
      "title": "Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling • Human Resources • Beloit College",
      "description": "Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Skip to main content Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. main content Open Side Nav Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Job Posting: Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Details Item Value Posting Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $80,000-84,000 per Year Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The opportunity Beloit College invites applications for a founding core faculty member in its new Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program. This is an opportunity to help build a program from the ground up and to shape its curriculum, teaching, and culture at a liberal arts institution that genuinely values faculty expertise and intellectual vision. We are seeking a counselor educator who understands that counselor education at its best is not just skills training: it is the formation of professionals who are theoretically grounded, socially aware, and equipped to work with the full complexity of human experience. Core faculty will teach across the CMHC curriculum, advise and mentor students, and contribute to the program’s CACREP accreditation, scholarship, and service. The program’s animating commitments include: social justice as a foundational orientation, embedded throughout the curriculum and clinical training; attention to underserved communities and the mental health workforce needs of south-central Wisconsin and the broader region, including Chicago, Milwaukee, and Madison; interprofessional and interdisciplinary education, consistent with Beloit’s institution-wide pedagogical identity; and community-based, experiential learning as a core program feature. About Beloit College Beloit College is a selective liberal arts college in Beloit, Wisconsin. Nationally recognized for intellectual rigor and innovation, Beloit was ranked #18 among the nation’s most innovative schools by U.S. News & World Report in 2026. Its graduates are known for their capacity to think across disciplines, engage with complexity, and connect knowledge to real-world impact. The School of Health Sciences, established in 2023, reflects Beloit’s commitment to preparing health professionals who are not only clinically excellent but broadly educated and community-minded. Interdisciplinary collaboration, experiential learning, and community-based practice are foundational to everything we do. The MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling is the School’s first graduate-level program, a significant milestone and a serious institutional commitment. Role and Responsibilities Core faculty serve as core counselor education faculty for the CMHC program, as defined under the 2024 CACREP Standards. This is a 12-month faculty position with teaching, advising, scholarship, and service responsibilities commensurate with the program’s needs. Core faculty report to the CMHC Program Director. Teaching and Curriculum Teach across the CMHC curriculum in areas of professional expertise, including foundational counseling coursework and one or more CACREP specialized practice areas Contribute to curriculum development, delivery, and continuous improvement consistent with the 2024 CACREP Standards Provide clinical instruction and supervision as assigned, in keeping with program policies Student Development and Gatekeeping Advise and mentor students, supporting professional identity development and well-being Participate in student assessment, retention, and gatekeeping processes consistent with ethical and professional standards Contribute to admissions and recruitment, especially for the first and second cohorts Scholarship, Service, and Accreditation Maintain sustained professional engagement through scholarship, professional development, service, advocacy, or ongoing counseling practice Contribute to CACREP self-study preparation, program evaluation, and ongoing compliance Represent the program in professional counseling organizations and collaborate across the School of Health Sciences and the broader College Required Qualifications Candidates must meet the 2024 CACREP core counselor education faculty requirements. Per CACREP Standards, core faculty hold a full-time appointment to the program and must have one of the following: An earned doctoral degree in counselor education, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program; or A related doctoral degree and full-time employment as a faculty member in a counselor education program for a minimum of one full academic year before July 1, 2013; or Full-time doctoral-level faculty employment in a CORE-accredited master’s program prior to July 1, 2017; or Graduation from a rehabilitation counseling doctoral program prior to January 1, 2018 In addition, all candidates must demonstrate the following per 2024 CACREP Standards: Sustained membership in professional counseling organizations Relevant professional counseling credentials (e.g., LPC, LCPC, or equivalent Wisconsin licensure or eligibility for Wisconsin licensure) Evidence of sustained professional engagement through professional development, service and advocacy, ongoing counseling practice, or research and scholarly activity in counseling Beyond CACREP requirements, Beloit College requires: Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching and evaluating student learning at the graduate level Demonstrated commitment to social justice, multicultural counseling, and working with marginalized and underserved communities Strong interpersonal and collaborative skills and the capacity to function effectively in a startup environment Preferred Qualifications Identification with the Clinical Mental Health Counseling specialized practice area (per CACREP Standards) Experience teaching in a CACREP-accredited program and familiarity with CACREP accreditation processes Experience with rural mental health, integrated behavioral health, or health disparities Background in interprofessional education or community-based training models Scholarly activity in areas aligned with the program’s mission Appointment and Compensation This is a full-time, 12-month core counselor education faculty position. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials through Beloit College’s online application system: Cover letter addressing qualifications and fit with the program’s mission Current curriculum vitae, including teaching, clinical, and scholarly experience Teaching philosophy statement Statement describing experience with and commitment to social justice and work with underserved communities Names and contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission) How to Apply Begin Your Application Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page Skip to main content This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! × May I help you? × Hi there! Do you have any questions?"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11182-founding-program-director-and-faculty-physician": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director and Faculty, Physician Assistant/Associate Studies",
      "description": "Founding Program Director and Faculty, Physician Assistant/Associate Studies  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Founding Program Director and Faculty, Physician Assistant/Associate Studies Job Posting: Founding Program Director and Faculty, Physician Assistant/Associate Studies Details Item Value Posting Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Salary Range $120,000-130,000 per Year Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description The opportunity Beloit College invites applications for a founding Program Director for its new Master of Science in Physician Assistant/Associate (PA) Studies program. This is an opportunity to build a program from the ground up, and to shape its identity, curriculum, and culture at a liberal arts institution that genuinely values faculty expertise and intellectual vision. The founding director will have significant latitude to develop a program that is both rigorously ARC-PA-compliant and distinctively Beloit. We are seeking a physician assistant leader who understands that PA education at its best prepares clinicians who are not only technically excellent but broadly educated, ethically grounded, and committed to serving communities in need. The program’s animating commitments include: attention to the primary care and health-workforce needs of south-central Wisconsin and the broader region; interprofessional and interdisciplinary education, consistent with Beloit’s institution-wide pedagogical identity; community-based clinical partnerships and experiential learning as core program features; and a commitment to serving diverse communities. About Beloit College Beloit College is a selective liberal arts college in Beloit, Wisconsin. Nationally recognized for intellectual rigor and innovation, Beloit was ranked #18 among the nation’s most innovative schools by U.S. News & World Report in 2026. Its graduates are known for their capacity to think across disciplines, engage with complexity, and connect knowledge to real-world impact. The School of Health Sciences, established in 2023, reflects Beloit’s commitment to preparing health professionals who are not only clinically excellent but broadly educated and community-minded. Interdisciplinary collaboration, experiential learning, and community-based practice are foundational to everything we do. The Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies will pursue accreditation from the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA), joining the School’s growing portfolio of graduate programs. Role and Responsibilities The Program Director is the physician assistant faculty leader responsible for the organization, administration, and continuous review and improvement of the PA program, as required under the ARC-PA Accreditation Standards for PA Education, Sixth Edition. This is a full-time, 12-month position, hired at 1.0 FTE, with at least 50% of that time devoted to administrative responsibilities for the program. The Program Director reports to the Director of the School of Health Sciences. Duties include but are not limited to: Program Development and ARC-PA Accreditation Lead all aspects of the ARC-PA provisional and ongoing accreditation process, including the self-study, application, and site visit, and ongoing compliance with the Sixth Edition Standards Maintain compliance with ARC-PA standards and establish continuous improvement initiatives. Develop and implement the program mission and learning outcomes, curriculum, program policies, student assessment and evaluation systems, and a comprehensive self-assessment and program evaluation plan Establish and cultivate clinical site partnerships across the region to ensure sufficient, high quality supervised clinical practice experiences Pursue state authorization and institutional approvals in coordination with institutional leadership and campus governance structures Support student recruitment and admissions, especially for the first cohorts Assist Communications and Marketing with the development and maintenance of high-quality, accurate internet content for the program’s web site Recommend instructional resources, including equipment, software, periodicals and textbooks to support instruction and learning Faculty and Program Leadership Recruit, hire, onboard, mentor, and evaluate principal faculty and staff, and coordinate with the Medical Director Provide program leadership through effective program organization, administration, communication, fiscal management, and continuous review and analysis Develop the student handbook, clinical handbook, and other program policies and infrastructure from the ground up Oversee student advising, assessment, progression, and remediation consistent with professional and ethical standards Develop admissions policies and procedures consistent with Beloit’s mission and core values as well current PA educational practices. Evaluate faculty performance and provide adequate support for faculty development. Service and Scholarship Establish an active, sustained program of scholarship in PA education, clinical practice, health workforce development or other area, including dissemination of scholarly work through peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, or funded research. Serve on School of Health Sciences and college-wide committees and participate actively in shared governance. Mentor junior faculty and support their professional and scholarly development Provide service to the profession through leadership, peer review, or volunteer roles with state or national PA organizations Community, Institutional Engagement, and Teaching Build and sustain relationships with clinical partners, preceptors, and community organizations Collaborate with faculty across the School of Health Sciences and the broader College to advance interprofessional programming Represent the program in professional state and national PA organizations and within the institution Teach in areas of professional expertise as needed by the program Assist College leadership with securing external funding for program support Required Qualifications Candidates must meet the ARC-PA program director requirements under the Accreditation Standards for PA Education, Sixth Edition. Specifically, the successful candidate must: Be a physician assistant who holds at least a Master’s degree and current or emeritus NCCPA certification status Hold current licensure, or be eligible for licensure, as a physician assistant in Wisconsin Have at least three years of full-time higher education experience at the time of appointment Be able to hold an academic appointment and privileges comparable to other faculty with similar responsibilities within the institution Be available to serve at 1.0 FTE on a 12-month, full-time basis, with at least 50% of that time devoted to administrative responsibilities Beyond ARC-PA requirements, Beloit College requires: Demonstrated leadership, administrative, and organizational skills, including budgeting and personnel management Demonstrated commitment to serving diverse communities Capacity to function effectively in a startup environment: the program does not yet exist, and the Director will build its infrastructure from the ground up Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree Experience founding, directing, or leading accreditation for a PA program, including direct involvement in ARC-PA processes Prior PA program administrative experience (program director, associate/assistant director, or academic/clinical coordinator) Experience with primary care, rural health, or health disparities Background in interprofessional education or community-based training models Scholarly activity aligned with the program’s mission Appointment and Compensation This is a full-time, 12-month administrative faculty position hired at 1.0 FTE, with at least 50% of that time devoted to program administration. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Per ARC-PA Standard D1.01(a), the Program Director must be hired on a permanent basis at least 15 months prior to the first day of the scheduled accreditation site visit; the anticipated start date is June 1, 2027. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials through Beloit College’s online application system: Cover letter addressing qualifications and vision for the program Current curriculum vitae, including administrative, teaching, and clinical experience Leadership statement (2–3 pages) describing experience with program development, accreditation, and faculty leadership Teaching philosophy statement Names and contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission) Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Begin Your Application Review of applications will begin in October, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/10985-program-director-and-faculty-clinical-mental": {
      "title": "Program Director and Faculty",
      "description": "Program Director and Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Program Director and Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program Job Posting: Program Director and Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program Details Item Value Posting Date 06/03/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Program Director (Founding) and Faculty, Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health Counseling The opportunity Beloit College invites applications for a founding Program Director for its new Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program. This is an opportunity to build a program from the ground up; to shape its identity, curriculum, and culture at a liberal arts institution that genuinely values faculty expertise and intellectual vision. The founding director will have significant latitude to develop a program that is both rigorously CACREP-compliant and distinctively Beloit. We are seeking someone who understands that counselor education at its best is not just skills training: it is the formation of professionals who are theoretically grounded, socially aware, and equipped to work with the full complexity of human experience. The program’s animating commitments include: Social justice as a foundational orientation, embedded throughout the curriculum and clinical training Attention to underserved communities and the urgent mental health workforce needs of south-central Wisconsin and the broader region, including Chicago, Milwaukee, and Madison Interprofessional and interdisciplinary education, consistent with Beloit’s institution-wide pedagogical identity Community-based connections and experiential learning as core program features, not afterthoughts About Beloit College Beloit College is a selective liberal arts college in Beloit, Wisconsin. Nationally recognized for intellectual rigor and innovation, Beloit was ranked #18 among the nation’s most innovative schools by U.S. News & World Report in 2026. Its graduates are known for their capacity to think across disciplines, engage with complexity, and connect knowledge to real-world impact. The School of Health Sciences, established in 2023, reflects Beloit’s commitment to preparing health professionals who are not only clinically excellent but broadly educated and community-minded. Interdisciplinary collaboration, experiential learning, and community-based practice are foundational to everything we do. This new MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling program will be the School’s first graduate-level offering, a significant milestone and a serious institutional commitment. Role and Responsibilities The Program Director serves as the core counselor education faculty leader for the CMHC program, as defined under 2024 CACREP Standard 1.FF. This is a 12-month administrative faculty position with teaching responsibilities commensurate with the Director’s expertise and program needs. The Program Director reports to the Director of the School of Health Sciences. Program Development and CACREP Accreditation Lead all aspects of the CACREP accreditation process, including curriculum development, self-study preparation, and ongoing compliance Develop and implement program policies, student assessment systems, key performance indicators, and a comprehensive program evaluation plan consistent with 2024 CACREP standards Establish and cultivate clinical placement partnerships across the region to ensure sufficient practicum and internship opportunities for students Pursue state program approval in coordination with institutional leadership Support and influence student recruitment and admissions into the program, especially for the first and second cohorts Faculty and Program Leadership Participate actively in recruiting, hiring, and onboarding 2–3 additional core and affiliate counselor education faculty members Provide ongoing leadership, mentorship, and evaluation for program faculty Coordinate advising, student assessment, retention, and gatekeeping processes consistent with ethical and professional standards Develop the student handbook, fieldwork handbook, and other program infrastructure from the ground up Community and Institutional Engagement Work collaboratively with program faculty and staff to build and sustain relationships with community partners, fieldwork site supervisors, and advisory committee members Collaborate with faculty across the School of Health Sciences and the broader College to advance interdisciplinary programming Represent the program in professional counseling organizations and within the institution Teach graduate courses in areas of professional expertise as needed by the program Required Qualifications Candidates must meet CACREP core counselor education faculty requirements per 2024 Standard 1.Y. Specifically, the successful candidate must have one of the following: An earned doctoral degree in counselor education, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program; or A related doctoral degree and full-time faculty employment in a counselor education program for a minimum of one full academic year before July 1, 2013; or Full-time doctoral-level faculty employment in a CORE-accredited master’s program prior to July 1, 2017; or Graduation from a rehabilitation doctoral program prior to January 1, 2018 In addition, all candidates must demonstrate the following per 2024 CACREP Standards 1.Z and 1.AA: Active membership in professional counseling organizations Relevant professional counseling credentials (e.g., LPC, LCPC, or equivalent licensure in Wisconsin or eligibility for Wisconsin licensure) Evidence of sustained professional engagement through at least two of the following: professional development in counseling, professional service and advocacy, ongoing counseling practice, or research and scholarly activity in counseling Beyond CACREP requirements, Beloit College requires: Demonstrated experience in counselor education program development, including direct involvement in CACREP accreditation processes Faculty experience in a graduate counseling program, including teaching, advising, and supervision Demonstrated commitment to social justice, multicultural counseling, and working with marginalized and underserved communities Strong interpersonal and administrative skills, including the ability to build relationships with community partners and collaborate across disciplines Capacity to function effectively in a startup environment: the program does not yet exist, and the Director will be building its infrastructure Preferred Qualifications Experience founding or relaunching an academic program Experience with rural mental health, integrated behavioral health, or health disparities Background in interprofessional education or community-based training models Experience recruiting and mentoring diverse graduate student populations Scholarly activity in areas aligned with the program’s mission Appointment and Compensation This is a full-time, 12-month administrative faculty position. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience, with a range of $85,000–$95,000. The anticipated start date is October 1, 2026. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials through Beloit College’s online application system: Cover letter addressing qualifications and vision for the program Current curriculum vitae, including administrative, teaching, and research experience. Leadership statement (2–3 pages) describing experience with program development, accreditation, faculty leadership, and clinical education Teaching philosophy statement Names and contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission) The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be construed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Beloit College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to building a diverse and inclusive faculty. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose backgrounds, identities, and experiences reflect the communities our program aspires to serve. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/10965-program-director-occupational-therapy-program": {
      "title": "Program Director, Occupational Therapy Program",
      "description": "Program Director, Occupational Therapy Program  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Program Director, Occupational Therapy Program Job Posting: Program Director, Occupational Therapy Program Details Item Value Posting Date 05/11/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Program Director (Founding), Master of Occupational Therapy Beloit College | School of Health Sciences Beloit College invites applications for a founding Program Director for its new Master of Occupational Therapy (OTM) program. This is an opportunity to build a program from the ground up at a nationally recognized liberal arts institution committed to intellectual curiosity, interdisciplinary thinking, and education that connects knowledge to real-world impact. The founding director will have significant latitude to shape the program’s identity, curriculum, and culture in alignment with Beloit’s distinctive liberal arts mission. The role will also require substantial entrepreneurial and foundational effort to stand up the program successfully and help pave the way for future graduate and professional programs at Beloit. About Beloit College Beloit College is a selective liberal arts college in Beloit, Wisconsin, known for its commitment to experiential learning, global engagement, and producing graduates who think across disciplines. Beloit College was ranked #18 for most innovative schools by US News and World Report in 2026. The School of Health Sciences, the site of our career-focused and liberal arts-centered health professions preparation, reflects these values, preparing students to become health professionals who are not only clinically excellent but broadly educated and community-minded. An OTM program at Beloit offers the opportunity to reimagine occupational therapy education through a liberal arts lens. Position Summary The Program Director will report to the Director of the School of Health Sciences and will hold an appointment with responsibilities in both program administration and teaching. The Program Director will lead all aspects of program development and launch, including curriculum design, faculty recruitment, clinical partnership development, and ACOTE accreditation. The successful candidate will bring a clear vision for developing a strong occupational therapy education in the context of the liberal arts and the leadership skills to bring that vision to life within a collaborative, student-centered academic community. The successful candidate will, once the program is accredited by ACOTE, provide administrative leadership for the program and will also serve as a core faculty member for the program in a dual academic and administrative appointment. This position is a renewable 12-month appointment. Responsibilities Program Development and Administration Lead all phases of OTM program creation and development, including curriculum design, policy development, and operational infrastructure. Recruit, hire, mentor, and evaluate core and associated faculty and staff. Oversee student recruitment, admissions, advising, and retention. Manage program budget and resources in collaboration with institutional leadership. Lead ACOTE candidacy and accreditation processes, including self-study, site visit preparation, and ongoing compliance. Develop and sustain clinical education partnerships to support fieldwork and experiential learning. Implement program evaluation and continuous quality improvement processes. Teaching Teach in areas of expertise as core faculty in the OT program. Scholarship and Service Maintain an active scholarly agenda appropriate to rank. Contribute to departmental, college, and professional service. Represent the program at state, regional, and national professional meetings. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities: Launch a new OTM program, the first of its kind at Beloit College . Serve as the designated Program Director in compliance with ACOTE Standard A.2.1. Provide leadership in planning, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement. Ensure compliance with ACOTE accreditation standards. Manage program budgeting and resources. Recruit, hire, mentor, and evaluate faculty. Oversee curriculum design and assessment, including DEIJ principles. Teach courses in the OT program relevant to expertise Support student advising and well-being. Represent the program internally and externally. Credentials and Experience: Doctoral degree from a USDE-recognized accredited institution. Licensed occupational therapist. Minimum 8 years of OT experience including clinical, administrative, and scholarly work. Minimum 4 years of postbaccalaureate-level teaching experience. Evidence of leadership, vision, and the ability to build programs and teams Preferred Qualifications Experience leading or contributing significantly to ACOTE accreditation processes Experience launching or substantially developing a new academic program Demonstrated commitment to interprofessional education and community-engaged practice Interest in integrating liberal arts values (interdisciplinary thinking, ethical reasoning, global awareness) into OT education Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to understand and appreciate the mission of a residential, liberal arts college and to work well in a fast-paced office, with diverse faculty, staff, students, alums, general public in a variety of situations. Ability to develop and contribute to learning and work environments welcoming to people from a diverse variety of backgrounds and experiences. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including grammar, punctuation, spelling, and proofreading. Flexibility and willingness to adapt to changing activities, expectations, and responsibilities. Excellent problem solving skills, with the ability to think critically, effectively prioritize, plan, and organize multiple tasks and projects and meet set deadlines without immediate and constant supervision. Knowledge of customer service standards and the ability to communicate effectively with faculty, administrators, staff, students, families of students, prospective students and their families, and the general public. Ability to maintain confidentiality and to safeguard the confidentiality of records. Willingness to look for improvements in personal and office performance and initiate proposals which enhance the work of the office. The intent of this job description is to provide the general nature and level of work required of employees who are assigned to this classification and shall not be constructed as an all-inclusive list of duties and responsibilities. Employees may be instructed to perform job-related duties and responsibilities other than those specifically presented in this description. How to Apply Application Materials Applicants should submit the following: Cover letter addressing qualifications and vision for the program Current curriculum vitae Leadership statement (2–3 pages) describing experience with the liberal arts, program development, accreditation, faculty leadership, and fiscal management Teaching philosophy statement Names and contact information for three professional references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission) Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is December 1, 2026. Begin Your Application Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/11124-visiting-assistant-professor-of-business-and": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Business and Psychology",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Business and Psychology  • Human Resources  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Human Resources Faculty & Staff Opportunities Student Job Openings Employee Resources Student Worker Resources Holiday Schedule Contact Us Home Human Resources Visiting Assistant Professor of Business and Psychology Job Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of Business and Psychology Details Item Value Posting Date 08/20/2026 Closing Date Until filled Employment Type(s) Full Time Location Beloit, Wisconsin, 53511 Description Beloit College invites applications from those with industrial-organizational psychology training and experience for a Visiting Assistant Professor of Business and Psychology position for the 2027-28 academic year. This is a benefits-eligible position and has the possibility of renewal. The successful candidate will teach 6 courses (3 each semester) including Introduction to Psychology, a course in our Psychological Research Methods and Statistics sequence, and intermediate courses in their area of expertise, such as Behavioral Economics, Consumer Behavior and Marketing, Industrial-Organizational Psychology, Organizational Management, Organizational Leadership, etc. We seek a colleague who has demonstrated excellence in or strong potential for teaching undergraduates, and whose pedagogies or research align with and engage our increasingly diverse student body and our interdisciplinary curriculum. A PhD in Industrial-Organizational Psychology or Applied Social Psychology, Organizational Behavior, Organizational Leadership, Program Evaluation, or a related field is preferred, though applications from advanced ABD applicants will also be considered. Located in a diverse community close to Madison, Milwaukee, and Chicago, Beloit is a selective undergraduate liberal arts college that attracts students from across the United States and the world. The college emphasizes excellence in teaching, learning beyond the traditional classroom, international perspectives, and collaborative research among students and faculty. It is recognized as one of the Colleges That Change Lives. How to Apply Begin Your Application Candidates should submit as one pdf an application that includes a cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy, a CV, and a sample of teaching evaluations if there is prior teaching experience. In addition, candidates should have 3 letters of recommendation sent by recommenders to Diep Phan, Director of School of Business at phand@beloit.edu. Review of complete applications will begin on October 16, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to Diep Phan, Director of School of Business: phand@beloit.edu or Suzanne Cox, Chair of Psychology: coxs@beloit.edu Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
    },
    "https://www.beloit.edu/live/profiles/9829-dr-gloria-bradley": {
      "title": "Associate Dean of StudentsCo-Director of the Weissberg Program in Human Rights and Social JusticeDirector of Restorative Justice Campus InitiativeTitle IX Coordinator",
      "description": "Gloria Bradley  • Student Success, Equity, & Community  • Beloit College Top of page Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Beloit College Deposit Visit Request Info Give Give News Calendar For Beloiters Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni Our Story Search Beloit College Search Beloit College Our student-athletes give it their all. Now it’s our turn to show up for them. Join us for our Athletic Day of Giving. Home Student Success, Equity, & Community Gloria Bradley Dr. Gloria Bradley, Ed.D. Associate Dean of Students Co-Director of the Weissberg Program in Human Rights and Social Justice Director of Restorative Justice Campus Initiative Title IX Coordinator Email: bradleyg@beloit.edu Phone: +1 608-363-2617 Office: Dean of Students office, 2nd floor, north side Pearsons Hall Student Success, Equity, & Community Grant Programs Weissberg Program Restorative Justice Practices Bias Incident Policy Contact Us Beloit College Offices & Services Employment Directions Privacy Policy Editor Login Follow Beloit College on Instagram Follow Beloit College on Facebook Follow Beloit College on X/Twitter Follow Beloit College on LinkedIn Follow Beloit College on YouTube 700 College St., Beloit, Wisconsin 53511 608-363-2000 © 2026 Beloit College. All Rights Reserved. Back to top of page This site uses cookies to improve your experience. Read our Web Privacy Policy for more information. Got it! ×"
